// TEST: ML Ops perm_weight_dim Bad N (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
import ml as ml
// ============================================================================
// The v1 S_n surface requires a STATIC N >= K + L
// (retired transforms-as-types plan §3.6, stage 5a). At N >= K + L the weight
// basis is the FULL partition lattice of the K+L axis positions, Bell(K+L)
// weights. Below it the lattice truncates to the partitions with at most N
// blocks — the partitions with more blocks than N have no witness tuple in
// [N]^{K+L} at all, so their coarsening indicators are identically zero and
// are not basis elements. Here K + L = 4 and N = 3: 14 weights, not 15.
//
// That truncated basis is perfectly sound arithmetic (the compiler's counting
// layer computes it, and the Perm Spec test block pins it), but it is a
// DIFFERENT convention: different count, different weight layout, different
// emitted kernel. §3.6's no-silent-fork rule says the surface must refuse
// rather than quietly switch, so the truncated-basis variant is a NAMED
// DEFERRAL and this is a compile-time error carrying both counts.
//
// The refusal reports through the BL3999 static-evaluation channel — a
// `let static` that cannot fold — exactly like ml-ops/015's K-cap probe. The
// ops (ml.derive_perm_linear / ml.derive_perm_bias, stage 5a-ii) will carry
// the identical text through the elaboration channel, from the same shared
// precondition, so the two can never drift.
// ============================================================================
let static BAD = ml.perm_weight_dim(2, 2, 3)
